HEADER='''Create a single-object 3D asset concept render for an original grim dark fantasy game. Show one complete subject in a neutral front three-quarter view, fully within frame with generous padding. Neutral mid-grey studio background, even soft white lighting, sharp surface description with readable shadows and natural material colors. Do not bake dramatic colored light into the design. No text, labels, watermark, game HUD, dramatic camera distortion, collage, multiple unrelated objects, stand, cast-shadow floor or scenery. Separate materials by believable construction. Show robust physically connected forms, intended negative spaces and sufficient thickness; fine wear belongs in the surface, not hundreds of detached specks. This is an object reference for image-to-3D, not an environment painting.\n\n'''
FOLLOW='''Using the approved image as the only design authority, render a true side view of the exact same object, unchanged proportions, silhouette details, material assignments and damage locations. Neutral matching studio lighting/background. One full object, no labels or other views. Do not redesign its hidden side. If the reference cannot determine a hidden construction detail, choose the simplest physically consistent continuation. Then repeat this request separately for a rear three-quarter view and visually compare for contradictions before using them as additional Rodin references.'''
